# AGENTS.md

{{synopsis}}. The owner reviews every change.
Write code that {{reader}} can read. Setup is in `README.md`.

## Checks

`scripts/check` runs every gate: ruff format, ruff check (all rules), a search for switched-off
checks and code that hides from them, mypy --strict, pytest with warnings as errors and no
skipped or uncollected tests, and 100 % branch coverage. The git hook and CI run it too.

- Work in small steps and keep `scripts/check` green after each one.
- Done means `scripts/check` is green. Show the command and the end of its output.
- When a check stays red after two honest attempts, stop and report what you tried.
- Fix the cause of a red check. Gate files change only with the owner's explicit approval:
  `scripts/check`, `.githooks/`, `.github/`, `.claude/`, `tests/conftest.py`, `.python-version`,
  `mise.toml`, `mise.lock`, the `[tool.*]` tables, `[build-system]`, `[project.entry-points]`
  and the `dev` group in `pyproject.toml`, and existing tests.

```sh
uv run pytest -k banner                         # one test by name (or tests/test_core.py::test_x)
uv run ruff format && uv run ruff check --fix   # format, then safe lint fixes
```

If uv says "Required uv version ... does not match", put `mise exec --` before the command.
`scripts/check` does that itself.

Sandboxed agents: uv writes to `~/.cache/uv` and `~/.local/share/uv`, and mise to its folders in
`.claude/settings.json`. A cold cache or a changed `uv.lock` needs the network (`pypi.org`,
`files.pythonhosted.org`, `releases.astral.sh`, `github.com`), and so does `gh`. Without these,
`scripts/check` fails for reasons outside the code.

## Python

Read `CODING_STANDARDS.md` before writing or reviewing Python.

The checks ban `print` outside `__main__.py`, relative imports, `Any`, TODO comments and
commented-out code. Every module and function has a Google-style docstring, and mypy needs an
annotation on every function. Do not use `cast`, `# noqa`, `# type: ignore`,
`contextlib.suppress`, skips, xfails, warning filters or the `recwarn` fixture: fix the cause.
Hypothesis settings live only in `tests/conftest.py`; run a state machine with
`run_state_machine_as_test(Machine)` in a plain test. `TYPE_CHECKING` appears only as
`if TYPE_CHECKING:`, with no `else` and only imports in it. Use `platform.system()`, not
`sys.platform`. A test never expects or catches `AssertionError`,
`Exception` or `BaseException`, and a test that catches a failing assert in any other way fails.
Library code never names `AssertionError`: raise a specific exception. pytest loads only the
plugins that `pyproject.toml` names. No code uses the plugin manager, `sys.monitoring`,
`warnings.filters`, `atexit`, `ctypes` or `os.exec*`/`os.spawn*`/`os.fork`. Coverage skips
only `if TYPE_CHECKING:`, `...` bodies, the `python -m` guard and `assert_never(x)`.

The editor language server is pyright. When pyright and mypy disagree, mypy wins: it is the gate.

## Layout

- Logic goes in the library under `src/{{module}}/`. `__main__.py` only calls it.
- Every `tests/test_*.py` file runs automatically. Python files go only in `src/{{module}}/`
  and `tests/`, in folders whose names do not start with a dot; `scripts/check` rejects them
  anywhere else. Vendored agent skills in `.agents/`
  are not project code, and the gates skip them.
- `.python-version` names the exact Python. uv installs it; never use a system Python.
- A new dependency needs the owner's approval. Then `uv add <name>` updates `pyproject.toml` and
  `uv.lock`. Commit both.

## Writing

For chat replies, commits, PRs, code comments and docs. Many readers are not native English
speakers.

- Short sentences and plain words. Lead with the result. Then what the reader needs to act: what
  changed, what failed, what is left, what you did not verify.
- Say what a technical idea does before you name it.
- A chat reply fits one screen. Use a table for parallel facts and a numbered list for steps.
  Keep every risk and open question.
- Name files by repo-relative path.
- Docs state rules and pointers, never project status. Status goes stale.
- Commits and PRs describe the change only, with no tool or AI attribution.
- PR title: `type(scope): what changed`, at most 72 characters. CI checks it. PR body: fill
  `.github/pull_request_template.md`, one line per slot. One concern per PR, about 200 changed
  lines at most. Open it with `gh pr create --assignee @me`, so the owner is assigned. Stack
  bigger work as PRs whose base is the branch below. Squash merges make the PR title and body the
  commit on `main`.

## Review

Review each PR on its own. Before a stack merges, review it once as a whole for problems between
PRs only:

```sh
git diff $(git merge-base origin/main <top>)..<top>
```
